[
  {
    "id": "sitl18-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 07 INT local vs global",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Proves DESIGN.md section 14: COMMAND_INT local-frame x/y scale as metres x 1e4, while global frames scale as degrees x 1e7. ArduPilot accepts DO_SET_HOME with GLOBAL_INT and denies LOCAL_NED; PX4 accepts both and decodes LOCAL_NED as metres.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl18-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl18-tab",
    "name": "COMMAND_INT frame matrix: GLOBAL_INT vs LOCAL_NED",
    "info": "Four one-shot DO_SET_HOME probes: ArduPilot GLOBAL_INT, ArduPilot LOCAL_NED, PX4 GLOBAL_INT, PX4 LOCAL_NED.\n\nGlobal cases enter latitude/longitude as decimal degrees and ride MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_INT (5) on msg.mavFrame from the inject: the dialog offers GLOBAL (0) as the only absolute-altitude spelling, and any other frame rides msg.mavFrame. Local cases enter x/y as metres in the same param slots and use MAV_FRAME_LOCAL_NED (1); the command node scales those to metres x 1e4 on COMMAND_INT.\n\nExpected result per DESIGN.md section 14: GLOBAL_INT ACCEPTED on both stacks; LOCAL_NED DENIED on ArduPilot and ACCEPTED on PX4.\n\nArduPilot Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550 -> remote 127.0.0.1:14551, sysid 1.\nPX4 Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14560 -> remote 127.0.0.1:14561, sysid 11.",
    "x": 310,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
